                "rationale": "Dopamine normally excites the direct pathway (via D1 receptors, promoting movement) and inhibits the indirect pathway (via D2 receptors). In Parkinson's, dopamine depletion reduces direct pathway activity and disinhibits the indirect pathway, excessively suppressing the motor thalamus (bradykinesia).",
