              "question": "A 22-year-old presents with asterixis, dysarthria, choreoathetosis, psychiatric changes, and golden-brown Kayser-Fleischer rings on slit-lamp exam. Serum ceruloplasmin is LOW and 24-hr urinary copper is HIGH. What is the diagnosis?",
