              "question": "A psychiatric patient treated with high-dose Haloperidol develops severe generalized 'lead-pipe' muscle rigidity, a temperature of 104 F (40 C), labile blood pressure, diaphoresis, and a serum creatine kinase of 25,000 IU/L. What is the specific muscle relaxant antidote indicated for this condition?",
