              "topic": "Sulfasalazine in Inflammatory Bowel Disease",
              "question": "Sulfasalazine is cleaved by colonic bacterial azoreductases into Sulfapyridine and 5-Aminosalicylic Acid (5-ASA / Mesalamine). Which component provides therapeutic anti-inflammatory action, and which causes systemic side effects?",
