              "question": "A 68-year-old Scandinavian patient undergoing routine cataract evaluation has grey-white dandruff-like fibrillar deposits arranged in a target or bull's eye configuration on the anterior lens capsule, and heavily pigmented trabecular meshwork with Sampaolesi line. What surgical complication is this patient at highest risk for during phacoemulsification?",
