              "topic": "Pigment Dispersion Syndrome",
              "question": "A 26-year-old myopic male presents with intermittent ocular pain and halos around lights after vigorous basketball training. Examination reveals a vertical spindle-shaped pigment deposit on the corneal endothelium and mid-peripheral radial iris transillumination defects. What is the vertical endothelial pigment line called?",
