              "question": "A 4-month-old infant is brought with marked bilateral photophobia, blepharospasm, epiphora (lacrimation), and corneal enlargement ('ox-eye'). Horizontal linear breaks in Descemet's membrane are observed on gonioscopy. What are these tears called, and what is the primary surgical procedure if the cornea is clear?",
