              "question": "A 65-year-old hypertensive male presents with sudden, painless, moderate visual loss. Funduscopic examination demonstrates massive, widespread flame-shaped retinal hemorrhages in all four quadrants, dilated tortuous retinal veins, and cotton-wool spots ('blood and thunder' / 'stormy sunset' appearance). What is the diagnosis?",
