              "topic": "Retinitis Pigmentosa & Bone-Spicule Pigmentation",
              "question": "A 20-year-old male presents with lifelong night blindness (nyctalopia) and progressive peripheral visual field constriction ('tunnel vision'). Fundus examination reveals waxy pallor of the optic disc, attenuated retinal arterioles, and characteristic perivascular 'bone-spicule' pigmentation in the mid-periphery. What is the diagnosis?",
