              "exam_source": "NEET PG High-Yield Practice (NBE / AIIMS Pattern)",
              "topic": "Retinoblastoma: Leukocoria & Flexner-Wintersteiner Rosettes",
              "question": "An 18-month-old infant is brought to the clinic because the parents noticed a white pupillary reflex ('cat's eye reflex' / Leukocoria) in flash photographs. Histopathological examination of the enucleated eye demonstrates Flexner-Wintersteiner rosettes. What tumor is this?",
