              "question": "A 72-year-old smoker notices distortion of straight lines (Metamorphopsia on Amsler grid test) and rapid central vision loss in his right eye. Optical coherence tomography (OCT) reveals subretinal neovascularization with fluid accumulation originating from the choroid through Bruch's membrane. What is the first-line pharmacotherapy?",
