              "question": "A 68-year-old poorly controlled diabetic male presents with agonizing deep ear pain (worse at night) and purulent otorrhea. Otoscopy reveals abundant granulation tissue at the junction of the bony and cartilaginous external auditory canal. Cranial nerve VII palsy is noted. What is the causative pathogen and diagnostic imaging?",
