              "question": "A 17-year-old boy has a solitary, smooth, trilobed polypoidal mass arising from the maxillary antrum and extending through the accessory ostium into the choana and nasopharynx. How does an Antrochoanal (Killian's) polyp differ from Ethmoidal polyps?",
