              "question": "A 34-year-old female with a history of childhood rheumatic fever presents with hemoptysis and palpitations. Cardiac auscultation reveals a loud S1, a sharp high-pitched opening snap (OS) shortly after S2, and a low-pitched mid-diastolic rumbling murmur with presystolic accentuation at the cardiac apex. What indicates greater severity of the mitral stenosis?",
