              "question": "A 24-year-old male with known WPW syndrome presents with palpitations. ECG reveals an irregular, wide-complex tachycardia with variable QRS morphologies and rates exceeding 250 bpm (pre-excited Atrial Fibrillation). Which of the following drugs is STRICTLY CONTRAINDICATED as it can precipitate ventricular fibrillation and cardiac arrest?",
