              "topic": "Infectious Diseases - Pneumonia CURB-65",
              "question": "A 68-year-old male presents with high fever, chills, cough productive of rust-colored sputum, and right-sided pleuritic chest pain. Chest X-ray reveals right lower lobe consolidation. Assessment shows: Confused and disoriented to time; Blood Urea Nitrogen (BUN) 28 mg/dL; Respiratory Rate 34 breaths/min; Blood Pressure 82/50 mmHg; Age 68. What is his CURB-65 score and recommended site of care?",
