              "question": "A 45-year-old patient with severe acute pancreatitis develops acute dyspnea 24 hours after admission. ABG reveals PaO2 = 62 mmHg on FiO2 = 0.8 (PaO2/FiO2 ratio = 77.5). Chest radiograph shows bilateral diffuse alveolar infiltrates. Echocardiogram reveals normal LV ejection fraction and normal left atrial pressure without volume overload. According to the Berlin definition, what is the severity of ARDS, and what is the lung-protective ventilation strategy?",
