              "topic": "Neurovascular Syndromes - Lateral Medullary (Wallenberg) Syndrome",
              "question": "A 54-year-old male presents with sudden-onset severe vertigo, nausea, vomiting, intractable hiccups, and difficulty swallowing (dysphagia). Neurological examination demonstrates:\n• Ptosis, miosis, and anhidrosis on the right side of the face\n• Loss of pain and temperature sensation on the RIGHT side of the face\n• Loss of pain and temperature sensation on the LEFT side of the trunk and extremities\n• Right-sided cerebellar ataxia (dysmetria and dysdiadochokinesia)\nWhich blood vessel is most commonly occluded?",
