              "question": "A 55-year-old male with decompensated cirrhosis and known ascites develops a low-grade fever (100.2 F), vague diffuse abdominal tenderness, and altered mental status. Diagnostic paracentesis yields cloudy fluid. Which of the following ascitic fluid parameters confirms the diagnosis of Spontaneous Bacterial Peritonitis (SBP), and what is the empirical antibiotic of choice?",
