                "high_yield_pearl": "Hemochromatosis: HFE gene (C282Y mutation). Classic Triad: Cirrhosis + Bronze skin + Diabetes mellitus ('Bronze Diabetes'). Transferrin saturation > 45-50% (earliest/best screening test). Prussion blue stain shows blue hemosiderin granules. Treatment of choice: Therapeutic Phlebotomy (chelation with Deferoxamine only if anemia/cardiac disease prevents phlebotomy). Risk of Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC) is increased 20- to 200-fold!"
