                "high_yield_pearl": "Clostridioides difficile: Antibiotic-associated diarrhea. Toxin A (enterotoxin) + Toxin B (cytotoxin). Pseudomembranous colitis: Raised yellowish mucosal plaques. First-line therapy: Oral Fidaxomicin or Oral Vancomycin (10 days). (NOTE: IV Vancomycin is INEFFECTIVE!). Recurrent CDI: Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT) is highly effective (> 90% cure). NEVER give antimotility agents (Loperamide -> risk of toxic megacolon!)."
