              "topic": "Hashimoto's Thyroiditis & Lymphoma Risk",
              "question": "A 44-year-old female presents with cold intolerance, weight gain, constipation, dry coarse skin, periorbital puffiness, delayed relaxation of deep tendon reflexes ('hung-up' ankle jerk), and a painless, rubbery, firm goiter. Serum TSH is 48 mIU/L and Free T4 is 0.3 ng/dL. High titers of which autoantibodies confirm Hashimoto's Thyroiditis, and what rare malignancy is this patient at increased risk for if the thyroid rapidly enlarges decades later?",
