              "topic": "Nephrotic Syndrome - Minimal Change Disease (MCD)",
              "question": "A 4-year-old child presents with generalized edema (anasarca), heavy proteinuria (urinary protein 4.8 g/24hr), severe hypoalbuminemia (serum albumin 1.8 g/dL), and hypercholesterolemia. Urinalysis shows 'Maltese Cross' lipid droplets under polarized light (oval fat bodies) and NO hematuria. Light microscopy of the renal biopsy appears completely normal. What is seen on Electron Microscopy, and what is the drug of choice?",
