              "question": "A 34-year-old HIV-positive male with IV drug use history presents with severe, steroid-resistant nephrotic syndrome and progressive renal insufficiency. Renal biopsy shows sclerosis and hyalinosis involving parts (segmental) of some (focal) glomeruli, with the collapsing variant noted on electron microscopy. Which of the following is strongly linked to FSGS, and what is the primary genetic risk factor in patients of African ancestry?",
