                "rationale": "Metabolic Alkalosis is categorized by Urinary Chloride into: (1) Saline-Responsive (Chloride-Depleted, Urine Chloride < 15-20 mEq/L): Caused by loss of gastric H+ and Cl- (Vomiting, nasogastric suction) or prior Diuretic therapy. Loss of chloride and extracellular volume activates aldosterone, which promotes renal H+ and K+ excretion ('Paradoxical Aciduria'). Infusion of 0.9% Normal Saline restores volume and chloride, shutting off aldosterone and completely correcting the alkalosis! (2) Saline-Resistant (Chloride-Expanded / Normovolemic, Urine Chloride > 20 mEq/L): Caused by autonomous mineralocorticoid excess (Primary Hyperaldosteronism, Cushing's, Renovascular HTN) or genetic tubular mutations (Bartter syndrome, Gitelman syndrome, Liddle syndrome). Does NOT respond to saline.",
