              "question": "A 24-year-old female presents with fatigue, polyarthralgia of the PIP and MCP joints without joint erosion on radiographs, a photosensitive erythematous rash over her cheeks and bridge of nose sparing the nasolabial folds, and bilateral ankle edema. Urinalysis shows 3+ proteinuria and active cellular casts. Which of the following autoantibodies has the highest specificity for Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE) and correlates strongly with lupus nephritis and disease activity flares?",
