              "exam_source": "NEET PG High-Yield Practice (NBE / AIIMS Pattern)",
              "topic": "Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE) - ACR/EULAR Criteria",
              "question": "A 24-year-old female presents with malar rash sparing nasolabial folds, photosensitivity, non-erosive polyarthritis of MCP and PIP joints, oral mucosal ulcers, and pleuritic chest pain. What is the most sensitive entry criterion for SLE, and which two autoantibodies are the most SPECIFIC for SLE?",
