                "rationale": "EULAR/ACR Criteria for Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE): Required Entry Criterion: Positive Antinuclear Antibody (ANA) titer >= 1:80 by immunofluorescence on HEp-2 cells (> 99% sensitive; a negative ANA essentially rules out SLE). Clinical domains: Cutaneous (malar rash, discoid rash, alopecia), Musculoskeletal (synovitis / Jaccoud arthropathy), Renal (proteinuria > 0.5 g/day, Class III/IV lupus nephritis), Neuropsychiatric (seizures, psychosis), Hematologic (leukopenia < 4,000, thrombocytopenia < 100,000, autoimmune Coombs-positive hemolytic anemia). Immunology domains: (1) Anti-dsDNA: Highly specific, titers fluctuate with and monitor disease activity and nephritis; (2) Anti-Smith (anti-Sm): Most SPECIFIC antibody for SLE (> 99%), targets core snRNPs (spliceosome); (3) Antiphospholipid antibodies; (4) Low complement C3 and C4.",
