              "topic": "Inflammatory Myopathies - Dermatomyositis",
              "question": "A 48-year-old female presents with progressive, symmetrical proximal muscle weakness (difficulty climbing stairs and combing hair), Gottron's papules (violaceous papules over knuckles and PIP joints), and a Heliotrope rash (violaceous erythema with periorbital edema of upper eyelids). Serum Creatine Kinase (CK) is 4,200 IU/L. What is the pattern of muscle biopsy inflammation, and what occult screening is mandatory?",
