                "rationale": "Modified Camitta Criteria for Severe Aplastic Anemia (SAA): Requires Bone Marrow Cellularity < 25% (or < 50% with < 30% hematopoietic cells) PLUS at least TWO of the following peripheral blood criteria: (1) Absolute Neutrophil Count (ANC) < 500 cells/uL, (2) Platelet count < 20,000/uL, (3) Absolute Reticulocyte Count < 20,000/uL (or reticulocytes < 1%). (If ANC < 200 cells/uL, it is categorized as Very Severe Aplastic Anemia / VSAA). Pathophysiology: T-cell mediated autoimmune destruction of CD34+ hematopoietic pluripotent stem cells (driven by IFN-gamma and TNF-alpha). Definitive Treatment of Choice: (1) Young patients (< 40-50 years) with an HLA-matched sibling donor: ALLOGENEIC HEMATOPOIETIC STEM CELL TRANSPLANTATION (HSCT, > 80-90% cure rate); (2) Older patients or those lacking an HLA-matched donor: Immunosuppressive Therapy (IST) with Horse Antithymocyte Globulin (ATG) + Cyclosporine + Eltrombopag (thrombopoietin receptor agonist).",
