              "topic": "Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC)",
              "question": "A 48-year-old female in septic shock from Gram-negative Escherichia coli pyelonephritis develops spontaneous oozing of blood from IV venipuncture sites, ecchymoses, and hematuria. Laboratory coagulation testing reveals: Platelet count = 35,000/uL, PT/INR = 2.4 (prolonged), aPTT = 58 seconds (prolonged), Plasma Fibrinogen = 65 mg/dL (markedly depressed < 100), and D-Dimer is markedly elevated at > 20 mcg/mL. What pathological process drives DIC, and what is the primary management priority?",
