              "topic": "Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia (APL / AML M3)",
              "question": "A 28-year-old female presents with severe epistaxis, oral mucosal bleeding, and ecchymoses. Complete blood count shows pancytopenia with 45% abnormal promyelocytes packed with heavy azurophilic granules and bundles of Auer rods ('Faggot Cells'). Coagulation testing reveals fulminant DIC (prolonged PT, low fibrinogen, high D-dimer). What cytogenetic translocation creates the PML-RARA fusion protein, and what molecular targeted therapy cures > 90% without conventional chemotherapy?",
