                "rationale": "The Parkland (Baxter) Formula calculates resuscitation fluid for burn patients with >= 20% TBSA deep partial-thickness or full-thickness burns: Total 24-hour Crystalloid (Ringer's Lactate) = 4 mL * Body Weight (kg) * % TBSA burned. (Note: Wallace Rule of Nines: Head 9%, Each Arm 9%, Anterior Trunk 18%, Posterior Trunk 18%, Each Leg 18%, Perineum 1%). Here: 4 * 70 * 36 = 10,080 mL of Ringer's Lactate. Timing Rule: Half of the total volume (5,040 mL) is infused over the first 8 hours calculated from the TIME OF INJURY (not time of hospital arrival!), and the remaining half is infused over the subsequent 16 hours. Resuscitation adequacy is monitored primarily by Urine Output: target 0.5 mL/kg/hr (30-50 mL/hr in adults).",
