                "high_yield_pearl": "Surgical Wound Classification: Class I (Clean): No tract entered (Hernia repair, Thyroidectomy). Class II (Clean-Contaminated): Tract entered under controlled conditions without spillage (Elective Cholecystectomy, Appendectomy, Bowel resection). Class III (Contaminated): Gross spillage from GI tract or fresh accidental trauma. Class IV (Dirty): Established pus, fecal peritonitis, devitalized tissue. Antibiotic Prophylaxis Rule: Single IV dose administered within 60 minutes BEFORE skin incision (within 120 mins for Vancomycin/Fluoroquinolones)!"
