              "topic": "Acute Appendicitis - Alvarado Score & Signs",
              "question": "A 21-year-old male presents with periumbilical pain that shifted to the right lower quadrant 12 hours later, accompanied by anorexia, nausea, fever (38.2 C), and localized tenderness at McBurney's point with rebound tenderness and leukocytosis (WBC 14,800/uL). His Alvarado score is 9. What clinical sign produces pain in the right lower quadrant upon palpation of the LEFT lower quadrant?",
