              "question": "A 72-year-old multiparous female presents with an agonizing, tender, non-reducible swelling in the groin below and lateral to the pubic tubercle, associated with vomiting and small bowel obstruction. What are the boundaries of the Femoral Canal, and why does a femoral hernia carry a dramatically high risk of strangulation (30-40%)?",
