              "topic": "Hemorrhoids - Grading & Management",
              "question": "A 44-year-old male presents with bright red, painless bleeding per rectum during defecation and mucosal prolapse that protrudes through the anus during bowel movements but REDUCES SPONTANEOUSLY upon standing up. What grade of internal hemorrhoids is this, and what is the office-based procedure of choice?",
