                "high_yield_pearl": "Choledochal Cysts: Congenital duct dilatation. Female predilection. Anomalous Pancreatico-Biliary Junction (APBJ). Triad: Pain + Jaundice + Palpable Mass. Todani Classification: Type I = Extrahepatic fusiform (85% - commonest!); Type II = Diverticulum; Type III = Choledochocele; Type IV = Multiple intra/extrahepatic; Type V = Caroli's disease (pure intrahepatic). Malignancy Risk = High risk of CHOLANGIOCARCINOMA! Definitive Surgery: Complete surgical cyst excision + Roux-en-Y Hepaticojejunostomy."
