                "high_yield_pearl": "Pancreatic Pseudocyst Master Rules: Wall lacks epithelial lining (lined by fibrous tissue!). Requires 4-6 WEEKS for wall maturation. Complications: Infection (Pancreatic abscess), Rupture (pancreatic ascites), Hemorrhage (erosion into splenic artery -> Pseudoaneurysm!). Treatment of Choice: EUS-Guided Endoscopic Cystogastrostomy. External percutaneous drainage is avoided (leads to chronic pancreaticocutaneous fistula!)."
