                "rationale": "During percutaneous (PAIR) or surgical interventions for Hydatid Cysts (Echinococcus granulosus), scolicidal agents are instilled into the cyst cavity to kill live protoscolices and prevent secondary dissemination. Crucial Surgical Safety Rule: Prior to injecting ANY scolicidal agent, the surgeon/radiologist MUST aspirate and verify the absence of bile (confirming NO communication between the cyst cavity and the biliary tree!). SCOLICIDAL AGENT TOXICITY: FORMALIN (Formaldehyde), Absolute Alcohol, and Hydrogen Peroxide are POTENT CAUSTIC SCLEROSING AGENTS. If they enter the biliary tree through a cysto-biliary fistula, they trigger fulminant chemical erosion, widespread ductal necrosis, and irreversible, catastrophic SECONDARY SCLEROSING CHOLANGITIS (resembling end-stage PSC, requiring liver transplantation!). The preferred, safe scolicidal agent of choice is HYPERTONIC SODIUM CHLORIDE (15-20% Saline for 15-20 minutes).",
