                "high_yield_pearl": "Breast Cancer Triple Assessment: (1) Clinical Exam, (2) Mammography / Ultrasound, (3) Core Needle Biopsy (CNB). CNB is preferred over FNAC (distinguishes in-situ from invasive cancer + tests ER, PR, HER2, Ki-67). BI-RADS 4 and 5 require Biopsy! Most common breast cancer = Invasive Ductal Carcinoma (IDC, 75-80%). Most common site = Upper Outer Quadrant (50%)."
