              "topic": "Paget's Disease of the Nipple vs Eczema",
              "question": "A 56-year-old female presents with persistent, unilateral, crusting, scaling, and erythematous weeping of the nipple and areola, associated with burning and itching. Application of topical hydrocortisone for 3 months produces zero improvement. Full-thickness nipple biopsy reveals large, pale, vacuolated intraepithelial cells with mucin droplets scattered along the basal layer (Paget Cells). What underlying breast pathology is present in > 95% of patients with Paget's Disease of the Nipple?",
