                "high_yield_pearl": "Venous vs Arterial Ulcers Master Comparison: Venous Ulcers: MEDIAL MALLEOLUS ('Gaiter zone'). Shallow, irregular margins, granulation base, heavy exudate, Lipodermatosclerosis. Pulses are NORMAL. Pain RELIEVED by elevation! Mainstay of treatment = COMPRESSION BANDAGING / STOCKINGS + Endovenous Saphenous Ablation. Arterial Ulcers: Lateral toes, heel, bony pressure points. 'Punched out', well-demarcated edges, pale necrotic base, zero exudate. Pulses are ABSENT. Cold pale skin. Pain WORSE with elevation, relieved by hanging leg dependent! Compression is STRICTLY CONTRAINDICATED!"
