              "question": "A 58-year-old diabetic male presents with a deep, painless ulcer on the plantar aspect of his foot overlying the head of the first metatarsal, surrounded by a thick rim of hyperkeratotic callus. Sensation to 10g Semmes-Weinstein monofilament is completely absent, but both dorsalis pedis and posterior tibial pulses are strong and bounding. What type of ulcer is this, and what is the primary management strategy?",
