                "rationale": "Stages of Labor: (1) First Stage: From onset of regular painful contractions to full cervical dilatation (10 cm). Divided into Latent Phase (slow cervical effacement/dilation up to 4-5 cm) and Active Phase (rapid cervical dilatation at >= 1 cm/hr in primiparas, >= 1.2-1.5 cm/hr in multiparas); (2) Second Stage: From full cervical dilatation (10 cm) to complete delivery of the baby (normal duration up to 2-3 hours with epidural in nulliparas, up to 1-2 hours in multiparas); (3) Third Stage: From delivery of baby to complete expulsion of placenta and membranes (normal duration < 30 minutes); (4) Fourth Stage: The first 1-2 hours postpartum (critical observation for PPH). WHO MODIFIED PARTOGRAPH: Plotted ONLY when the woman enters the ACTIVE PHASE OF LABOR (cervical dilatation >= 4 cm). The ALERT LINE is drawn from 4 cm to 10 cm at a rate of 1 cm/hour. The ACTION LINE is drawn 4 HOURS TO THE RIGHT of and parallel to the Alert Line. If the cervical dilatation curve crosses to the right of the Alert line, it indicates prolonged labor (transfer to emergency obstetric facility); if it reaches or crosses the ACTION LINE, critical decision-making / intervention is mandatory (oxytocin augmentation, rupture of membranes, or Cesarean section for cephalopelvic disproportion).",
