              "question": "A 28-year-old primigravida has prolonged active labor. Vaginal examination reveals the fetal head in Right Occipito-Posterior (ROP) position. What is the most common natural outcome of the fetal head in persistent OP position, and what occurs if internal rotation arrests at 90 degrees?",
