                "rationale": "Face Presentation occurs when the fetal head is completely hyperextended, so that the occiput touches the back and the face presents. The presenting diameter is the SUBMENTO-BREGMATIC DIAMETER (9.5 cm, identical to suboccipitobregmatic in vertex!). The denominator is the MENTUM (Chin). Crucial Obstetric Rule: (1) MENTO-ANTERIOR (Chin anterior, 70-80%): The fetal chin rotates anteriorly beneath the maternal pubic symphysis. The submental region pivots around the lower border of the symphysis, and the face delivers VAGINALLY by flexion (chin, mouth, nose, eyes, and forehead emerge sequentially). Vaginal delivery is completely achievable! (2) PERSISTENT MENTO-POSTERIOR (Chin posterior, 20-30%): The chin rotates into the hollow of the sacrum. Because the fetal neck is already in extreme hyperextension, it CANNOT extend any further to pivot under the pubic symphysis, and the fetal chest and shoulders are forced into the pelvic inlet simultaneously with the head, creating ABSOLUTE MECHANICAL OBSTRUCTION. A PERSISTENT MENTO-POSTERIOR POSITION CANNOT DELIVER VAGINALLY—CESAREAN SECTION IS MANDATORY! Note: Ventouse (vacuum extraction) is STRICTLY CONTRAINDICATED in face presentation (causes facial nerve damage and eye trauma). External fetal scalp electrodes are also contraindicated.",
