                "high_yield_pearl": "Perineal Tears (Sultan Classification): Grade 1 = Mucosa/skin only. Grade 2 = Perineal body muscles (anal sphincter intact). Grade 3 = Anal Sphincter involved: 3a = < 50% EAS torn; 3b = > 50% EAS torn; 3c = Both EAS and IAS torn (rectal mucosa intact). Grade 4 = Anal Sphincter + ANORECTAL MUCOSA breached! OASIS Management: Operating room repair + Stool softeners + Prophylactic antibiotics (prevents rectovaginal fistula and fecal incontinence!). Mediolateral Episiotomy: Incision starts at fourchette and angles 45-60 degrees laterally towards ischial tuberosity (protects anal sphincter!)."
