              "question": "A 46-year-old female presents with postcoital vaginal bleeding. Examination reveals an exophytic 3.5 cm cervical mass extending into the upper two-thirds of the vagina, with clear, non-involved parametria and no hydronephrosis. Under FIGO 2018 staging, what is the stage and recommended definitive treatment?",
