                "high_yield_pearl": "Ovarian Cancer High-Yield Pearls: Most deadly gynecologic malignancy. High-Grade Serous Carcinoma (#1, 75%): Arises from Fallopian tube fimbria (STIC lesions!). BRCA1/2 and p53 mutations. Psammoma bodies. Tumor Marker = CA-125. Protective factors: Multiparity, Oral Contraceptive Pills (50% reduction!), Breastfeeding, Bilateral Salpingectomy. Risk of Malignancy Index (RMI) = Ultrasound score x Menopausal status x CA-125. Standard Treatment: Staging Laparotomy + PRIMARY CYTOREDUCTION (Debulking) to zero residual macroscopic disease (R0) + Platinum-Taxane Chemotherapy (Carboplatin + Paclitaxel) + PARP Inhibitors (Olaparib) for BRCA mutants."
