              "topic": "Pelvic Inflammatory Disease (PID) - CDC Criteria & Fitz-Hugh-Curtis",
              "question": "A 22-year-old sexually active female presents with acute lower abdominal pain, purulent cervical discharge, and severe right upper quadrant pleuritic pain on deep inspiration. Pelvic examination reveals exquisite Cervical Motion Tenderness ('Chandelier Sign') and bilateral adnexal tenderness. Laparoscopy demonstrates purulent pelvic peritonitis and fine, fibrous 'Violin-String' adhesions between the anterior liver surface and the abdominal wall. What eponymous syndrome is this, and what empirical antibiotic regimen is recommended by the CDC for outpatient PID?",
