                "rationale": "Borderline Ovarian Tumors (BOTs / Tumors of Low Malignant Potential / Atypical Proliferative Tumors): Account for 10-15% of all epithelial ovarian neoplasms, occurring classically in young reproductive-age women (mean age 40). Histopathological Criteria: Displays features intermediate between benign cystadenomas and invasive carcinomas: (1) Epithelial stratification, (2) Cellular pleomorphism and nuclear atypia, (3) Budding of epithelial tufts, and (4) Increased mitotic figures; BUT WITH THE ABSOLUTE HALLMARK OF COMPLETE ABSENCE OF FRANK DESTRUCTIVE STROMAL INVASION. Biological Behavior: Indolent course with excellent overall survival (> 95-99% at 10 years). Surgical Management: In young women desiring future fertility, FERTILITY-SPARING SURGERY (Unilateral Salpingo-Oophorectomy or cystectomy with peritoneal staging) is completely safe and standard of care! Adjuvant chemotherapy provides ZERO survival benefit and is strictly NOT recommended.",
