              "id": "PEDS_PYQ_001",
              "question_type": "PYQ",
              "exam_source": "NEET PG 2024 Recall",
              "topic": "Neonatology - NRP Resuscitation Steps",
              "question": "A full-term newborn infant is delivered via emergency cesarean section for fetal distress. At birth, the infant is apneic, limp, and the heart rate is 54 bpm despite initial steps of warming, drying, and tactile stimulation. What is the immediate first action under Neonatal Resuscitation Program (NRP 8th Edition) guidelines?",
              "options": {
                "A": "Initiate Positive Pressure Ventilation (PPV) with room air (21% O2) via mask at 40 to 60 breaths/min",
                "B": "Initiate immediate chest compressions",
                "C": "Administer intravenous Epinephrine",
                "D": "Administer 100% free-flow oxygen via blow-by"
              },
              "correct_option": "A",
              "explanation": {
                "rationale": "Under NRP guidelines, if a newborn is apneic or gasping OR has a heart rate < 100 bpm after initial steps (warming, positioning, clearing secretions, drying, tactile stimulation) within the first 60 seconds ('The Golden Minute'), the SINGLE MOST IMPORTANT AND EFFECTIVE ACTION is the immediate initiation of POSITIVE PRESSURE VENTILATION (PPV) at 40-60 breaths/min. In term infants, PPV is initiated with 21% O2 (room air). Chest compressions are indicated ONLY IF heart rate remains < 60 bpm despite at least 30 seconds of EFFECTIVE PPV that moves the chest (MR. SOPA corrective steps).",
                "distractor_analysis": {
                  "A": "Correct. Under NRP guidelines, if a newborn is apneic or gasping OR has a heart rate < 100 bpm after initial steps (warming, posi...",
                  "B": "Incorrect choice for this clinical presentation (Initiate immediate chest compressions).",
                  "C": "Incorrect choice for this clinical presentation (Administer intravenous Epinephrine).",
                  "D": "Incorrect choice for this clinical presentation (Administer 100% free-flow oxygen via blow-by)."
                },
                "high_yield_pearl": "NRP 8th Edition Golden Rules: Apnea / Gasping OR Heart Rate < 100 bpm -> START POSITIVE PRESSURE VENTILATION (PPV) immediately! Initial FiO2: Term (>= 35 wks) = 21% O2; Preterm (< 35 wks) = 21-30% O2. Chest compressions indicated ONLY IF HR < 60 bpm AFTER 30 seconds of effective PPV with chest movement! Compression-to-ventilation ratio = 3:1."
              },
