              "topic": "Rh Hemolytic Disease of the Newborn (Erythroblastosis Fetalis)",
              "question": "An Rh-negative (D-negative) mother delivers her second child, who is Rh-positive. The mother did not receive anti-D immunoglobulin during her first pregnancy. The neonate is born pale, severely hydropic with hepatosplenomegaly, and develops rapidly rising jaundice within 6 hours. What laboratory finding is diagnostic, and how does Rh alloimmunization occur?",
