              "question": "A healthy term infant born to a blood group O-positive mother is found to have mild jaundice at 20 hours of life. The infant's blood group is A-positive. Blood smear reveals prominent Microspherocytes and polychromasia. Direct Coombs test is weakly positive. Why can ABO incompatibility affect the FIRST-BORN child, unlike Rh incompatibility?",
