                "high_yield_pearl": "PDA Master Pearls: Failure of ductus to close -> Aortic-to-pulmonary runoff. Murmur = CONTINUOUS 'MACHINERY' (GIBSON) MURMUR at left infraclavicular area. Physical Signs = BOUNDING PULSES + WIDE PULSE PRESSURE. Medical Closure in Preterms = IV IBUPROFEN or INDOMETHACIN (or Paracetamol). Keeping Ductus Open in Ductal-Dependent CHD = PROSTAGLANDIN E1 (Alprostadil)! Term infant PDA does NOT respond to NSAIDs."
