                "high_yield_pearl": "Coarctation of Aorta Summary: Juxtaductal narrowing. Cardinal Triad: (1) Upper limb HYPERTENSION + Lower limb HYPOTENSION, (2) RADIO-FEMORAL DELAY, (3) Exertional claudication. CXR: 'FIGURE OF 3' sign + INFERIOR RIB NOTCHING (Roesler sign, ribs 3-8). Associated with: BICUSPID AORTIC VALVE (80%) and TURNER SYNDROME! Emergency in neonates = IV Prostaglandin E1 to reopen ductus."
