              "topic": "Anterior Shoulder Dislocation - Bankart & Hill-Sachs Lesions",
              "question": "A 24-year-old rugby player sustains a violent blow to an abducted and externally rotated shoulder. He presents with severe shoulder pain, flattened deltoid contour ('Epaulette Sign'), an empty glenoid fossa with a prominent acromion, and the inability to touch the contralateral shoulder with the elbow resting against the chest (Dugas' Test positive). What two classic bony-labral lesions are pathognomonic of recurrent anterior glenohumeral instability?",
