              "topic": "Colles vs Smith vs Barton Fractures",
              "question": "An elderly osteoporotic female falls on an outstretched hand with the wrist extended, sustaining an extra-articular distal radius fracture with dorsal displacement, dorsal tilt, and radial shift producing a classic 'Dinner-Fork Deformity'. In contrast, what is the mechanism, displacement, and deformity seen in a Smith's Fracture?",
