                "high_yield_pearl": "Hip Dislocation High-Yield Distinction: POSTERIOR DISLOCATION (#1, 90%): 'Dashboard injury'. Limb locked in: FLEXION + ADDUCTION + INTERNAL ROTATION + Shortened! Nerve injured = SCIATIC NERVE. ANTERIOR DISLOCATION (10%): Limb locked in: ABDUCTION + EXTERNAL ROTATION. GOLDEN EMERGENCY RULE: Must reduce hip WITHIN 6 HOURS to prevent Avascular Necrosis (AVN) of femoral head! (Bigelow or Allis reduction maneuvers)."
