              "question": "A 30-year-old male falls asleep with his arm draped over the back of a park bench after heavy alcohol intoxication ('Saturday Night Palsy'). He awakens unable to extend his wrist or fingers. Physical examination confirms complete Wrist Drop and Finger Drop, but triceps reflex and elbow extension are completely preserved. Sensory loss is restricted to the first dorsal web space. At what anatomical level is the radial nerve compressed?",
