                "high_yield_pearl": "Chondroblastoma (Codman Tumor) Master Pearls: Skeletally immature youth (10-20 yrs). Strictly EPIPHYSEAL (proximal humerus & knee). Radiograph = Well-defined lytic lesion WITH SCLEROTIC RIM + internal calcifications. Histopathology Hallmark = PATHOGNOMONIC 'CHICKEN-WIRE' / 'LACE-LIKE' PERICELLULAR CALCIFICATION! Epiphyseal Bone Tumors: Chondroblastoma (< 20 yrs) vs Giant Cell Tumor (> 20 yrs)."
