                "high_yield_pearl": "SCFE Master Pearls: Obese adolescent boy (11-15 yrs) with REFERRED KNEE PAIN and limp! Hip exam = Obligatory External Rotation on flexion. Radiograph: KLEIN'S LINE DOES NOT INTERSECT EPIPHYSIS (Trethowan sign) + 'Ice cream slipping off cone'. Urgent Treatment = IN-SITU PERCUTANEOUS SCREW FIXATION. Avoid closed reduction (causes Avascular Necrosis!)."
