                "high_yield_pearl": "Ankylosing Spondylitis Master Guide: Young males (15-35 yrs). HLA-B27 positive (> 90%). Inflammatory back pain: Morning stiffness that IMPROVES WITH EXERCISE! MODIFIED SCHOBER TEST (< 5 cm expansion = reduced lumbar flexion). Radiograph = BILATERAL SYMMETRICAL SACROILIITIS + 'BAMBOO SPINE' (marginal syndesmophytes). #1 Extra-articular sign = ACUTE ANTERIOR UVEITIS (25%). First-line DOC = Continuous NSAIDs -> Anti-TNF biologics."
