                "high_yield_pearl": "Pityriasis Versicolor Summary: Causative agent = MALASSEZIA FURFUR / GLOBOSA (lipophilic yeast). Hot humid weather, upper back/chest. Hypopigmented macules fail to tan due to AZELAIC ACID INHIBITING TYROSINASE! Wood's lamp = Golden-yellow fluorescence. 10% KOH = PATHOGNOMONIC 'SPAGHETTI AND MEATBALLS' (short hyphae + round spores). Treatment = 2% Ketoconazole shampoo or Selenium Sulfide."
