                "high_yield_pearl": "Malignant Melanoma Master Guide: ABCDE Criteria: Asymmetry, Border notched, Color variegation, Diameter > 6 mm, EVOLVING (#1 clinical warning!). #1 Most Common Subtype = Superficial Spreading (70%). Acral Lentiginous Melanoma = Most common in Dark-Skinned individuals (palms, soles, subungual; NOT UV-related!). THE #1 PROGNOSTIC FACTOR = BRESLOW DEPTH (measured in mm to deepest cell!). Surgical margins: <= 1 mm = 1 cm; > 2 mm = 2 cm margin + SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSY (SLNB). BRAF V600E mutation -> Dabrafenib + Trametinib."
