                "high_yield_pearl": "Genital Ulcers Master Differential Table: (1) CHANCROID: Haemophilus ducreyi. EXQUISITELY PAINFUL + SOFT ULCER with ragged undermined edges + 'School of Fish' gram-negative rods + Suppurative Bubo. DOC = Azithromycin 1g. (2) LGV: Chlamydia L1-L3. Painless small papule -> Huge painful nodes with 'GROOVE SIGN' OF GREENBLATT (Poupart's ligament groove!). DOC = Doxycycline 21 days. (3) DONOVANOSIS: Klebsiella granulomatis. PAINLESS, BEEFY-RED VELVETY ULCERS + PSEUDOBUBO (No true adenopathy!). Crush smear = 'DONOVAN BODIES' (Safety-pin appearance inside histiocytes). DOC = Azithromycin."
