              "exam_source": "NEET PG High-Yield Practice (NBE / AIIMS Pattern)",
              "topic": "Frontotemporal Dementia (Pick's Disease)",
              "question": "A 56-year-old female presents with progressive personality changes, hyperorality, socially inappropriate disinhibited behavior, and apathy, while her spatial orientation and memory remain remarkably preserved. Brain MRI reveals bilateral frontal and anterior temporal atrophy. What is the diagnosis?",
