              "topic": "Chest Radiology - Silhouette Sign & Lobar Anatomy",
              "question": "A 54-year-old male presents with high fever, cough, and right-sided pleuritic chest pain. Posteroanterior (PA) chest radiograph reveals a homogeneous wedge-shaped opacity in the lower thoracic zone that completely obliterates the right cardiac border (right atrial margin), while the right hemidiaphragmatic contour remains sharply defined. What is this radiographic sign, and which specific pulmonary lobe is collapsed or consolidated?",
