              "question": "A trauma victim in the intensive care unit undergoes a portable supine chest radiograph. A deep, abnormally lucent, deepened costophrenic angle is seen extending laterally and inferiorly on the right side. What is this sign, and what pathology does it indicate in a supine patient?",
