              "topic": "Acute Pancreatitis - Contrast CT & Necrosis Assessment",
              "question": "A 45-year-old alcoholic male with severe acute pancreatitis undergoes dynamic contrast-enhanced CT on day 4 of admission to evaluate for complications. Non-enhancement of more than 50% of the pancreatic parenchyma is observed. Under the Balthazar and Revised Atlanta classifications, what does parenchymal non-enhancement denote?",
