                "rationale": "Intravenous contrast-enhanced CT performed after 72 hours of disease onset is the gold standard for diagnosing and quantifying pancreatic parenchymal necrosis. Viable pancreatic tissue enhances intensely, whereas unenhanced, devitalized areas with attenuation < 30-50 HU represent necrotizing pancreatitis. Parenchymal necrosis > 50% carries high mortality and morbidity.",
