              "topic": "Focal Liver Lesions - Hemangioma vs HCC vs FNH",
              "question": "A triphasic contrast CT of the liver in an asymptomatic 38-year-old female reveals a well-defined 3 cm liver lesion that demonstrates early peripheral, nodular, discontinuous enhancement during the arterial phase with progressive, centripetal (inward) fill-in on portal venous and delayed phases, becoming completely isodense to liver parenchyma. What is the diagnosis?",
