              "topic": "Renal Cyst Bosniak Classification",
              "question": "A 58-year-old male undergoes abdominal CT for trauma. An incidental 4 cm well-defined renal cyst is identified with a hairline-thin wall, no calcifications, no septations, and homogeneous water attenuation (6 HU) with zero contrast enhancement (< 10 HU increase). According to the Bosniak classification, what is the category and management?",
