              "question": "An intubated asthmatic patient undergoing laparoscopy suddenly develops high peak airway pressures. The capnography display shows a prolonged, sloped phase II and phase III with loss of the normal rectangular plateau, creating a classic 'shark-fin' waveform. What pathological process does this characteristic capnogram indicate?",
