              "question": "A 26-year-old primigravida develops a severe, throbbing bilateral fronto-occipital headache 24 hours after an uneventful Cesarean delivery under spinal anesthesia. The headache is markedly aggravated by sitting or standing upright and is completely relieved when lying flat supine. What needle characteristic minimizes this complication, and what is the definitive intervention for severe refractory PDPH?",
