              "question": "A trauma victim receives 6 liters of 0.9% Normal Saline during acute resuscitation. Arterial blood gas demonstrates a normal anion gap metabolic acidosis with hyperchloremia (serum Cl- 118 mEq/L) and a decreased base excess. Why does rapid massive resuscitation with 0.9% Normal Saline cause metabolic acidosis?",
