              "question": "A 50-year-old female undergoes a 4-hour laparoscopic hysterectomy in the lithotomy position. On postoperative day 1, she complains of numbness over the anterolateral leg and dorsum of the foot with inability to dorsiflex the foot ('foot drop'). Which peripheral nerve was compressed against the metal stirrup during lithotomy positioning?",
